      "dcterms:title": "SL2 tilting modules in the mixed case",
      "dcterms:creator": [
        "LOUISE SUTTON, DANIEL TUBBENHAUER, PAUL WEDRICH",
        "JIERUZHU"
      ],
      "dcterms:identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.07724",
      "dcterms:abstract": "Using the non-semisimple Temperley–Lieb calculus, we study the additive and monoidal structure of the category of tilting modules for SL2 in the mixed case. This simultane- ously generalizes the semisimple situation, the case of the complex quantum group at a root of unity, and the algebraic group case in positive characteristic. We describe character formulas and give a presentation of the category of tilting modules as an additive category via a quiver with relations. Turning to the monoidal structure, we describe fusion rules and obtain an explicit recursive description of the appropriate analog of Jones–Wenzl projectors.",
      "dcterms:source": "library/arxiv-2105.07724v2/manifest.jsonld",
      "dcterms:hasVersion": "library/arxiv-2105.07724v2"
    }
  ]
